  {
    "episode_id": 74498,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/4/74498.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 37,
    "turn_text": "Congressman, I mean, there's no shortage of topics to talk about today. And you've been really busy on a number of fronts for Louisiana, including the fishermen, but even when broader policy issues. Wanted to get your thoughts on Worda, Water Resources Development Act. I know you've worked on that for a large part of your career and there's just been significant movement. I believe the House passed a version of Worda and the Senate did as well. But where are things on Worda and can you highlight some of the big wins that you've helped shepherd for Louisiana?",
