    "turn_idx": 53,
    "turn_text": "Well, this is the last thing I'll have to say and this is personal privilege because it's our show and I can say what I want, but I just wanted to thank you for LA one. I'm a member of the LA one executive committee many people know that I share an office and. have spent 15 years of my life with Henri Bouet. But I think there was a huge win to get a grant to round out the money that was needed for the elevated highway. And I think people may or may not realize how long you have had a role in championing that project, right? From when you worked in other congressman's office, and now you are the congressman, I don't want that to go unsaid because I'm looking forward to standing next to you when we cut some ribbons. We will stand in front of Roy P. Francis, so he does not get to stand in the front anymore, but I'm looking forward to that day and I just wanted to thank you for that. For all your efforts to, you know, it's about connecting industry, but it is about connecting to our coast and frankly has a lot to do with with changing worlds and why we have to elevate the road to begin with. So thank you, thank you for your decades of work on LA1.",
